---
description: Global architecture rules for Expo hybrid finance app
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Tech Stack
- React Native Expo Router (TypeScript)
- Navigation: Expo Router (File-based)
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind CSS)

## UI Composition
- Atomic Design:
  - components/ui → atomic UI primitives
  - components/features → composed UI blocks
  - app/ → screens (via Expo Router)

## Core Principles
- Cross-Platform: Always ensure UI works on both Android and iOS.
- Screens are orchestration layers only.
- No monolithic components.
- Offline-first (SQLite / local storage).
- Business identifiers and invariants must live in `src/domain/constants`.
- Generic `constants.ts` is not allowed.

## File Size Rule
- >150 lines → extract to features/

## Global Architecture Rules (Non-Negotiable)

- The `app/` folder MUST contain only routes and screen components.
- No business logic, services, repositories, hooks, or utils may be created inside `app/`.

- Domain models MUST live in `src/domain/models`.
- Domain service interfaces MUST live in `src/domain/services`.

- Service and repository IMPLEMENTATIONS must live ONLY in:
  - `src/services/impl`
  - `src/repositories/*`

- The file `src/container.ts` is the ONLY composition root.
  - Only `container.ts` may instantiate services or repositories.
  - No other file may use `new Service()` or `new Repository()`.

- `container.ts` MUST NOT be imported by:
  - service implementations
  - repository implementations
  - domain models

- Respect dependency direction (imports): db ← repositories ← services ← domain.
- Respect runtime flow (execution-time): UI/hooks → container → services → repositories → db.

- Major architectural work must be tracked in docs/todo.md using checklists.
